  "reasoning": "Arizona\u2019s statewide Cook Partisan Voting Index is R+2, meaning it has voted about 2 points more Republican than the national average in recent presidential elections, despite currently having a Democratic governor and two Democratic U.S. senators[1][9]. In 2024, Donald Trump carried Arizona for president by 52.2% to 46.7% (a 5.5\u2011point Republican margin), while Democrat Ruben Gallego won the U.S. Senate race 50.1% to 47.7% (a 2.4\u2011point Democratic margin)[9]. Recent 2026 coverage describes Arizona as a swing/battleground state with Republicans holding a modest registration edge but competitive statewide races and no clear consensus among major forecasters on a decisive advantage for either party[5][6][11][16], so with current-cycle signals but no fresh head\u2011to\u2011head polling, the state is best characterized as a genuine toss\u2011up leaning neither clearly D nor R in federal contests.",
